steps.message:
The bug was that `rich/progress.py` printed a blank line in the `stop` method even when the progress display was disabled. I added a check `if not self.disable:` to the `stop` method to make it symmetric with the `start` method.

```python
    def stop(self) -> None:
        """Stop the progress display."""
        if not self.disable:
            self.live.stop()
            if not self.console.is_interactive and not self.console.is_jupyter:
                self.console.print()
```
